The U.S. state of [[Iowa]] first required its residents to register their [[motor vehicle]]s in 1904. Registrants provided their own [[Vehicle registration plate|license plates]] for display until 1911, when the state began to issue plates.<ref>{{cite news |last=Swarm |first=Curt |date=February 15, 2013 |title=Moulton man has 100-year collection of Appanoose County license plates |url=http://www.dailygate.com/opinion/article_43262419-45c6-5bb9-9e92-703e3afa725d.html |newspaper=Daily Gate City |location=Keokuk, IA |access-date=September 23, 2016}}</ref>

Plates are currently issued by the [[Iowa Department of Transportation]] through its Motor Vehicle Division. Front and rear plates are required for most classes of vehicles, while only rear plates are required for motorcycles and trailers.

